WEBVTT

00:17:28.083 --> 00:17:30.059
It is the foundation of trust.

00:17:30.083 --> 00:17:32.809
You will exist inside of me
when you're not there,

00:17:32.833 --> 00:17:35.643
and I exist inside of you
when I am not there.

00:17:35.667 --> 00:17:37.809
And therefore,
I don't need to check on you

00:17:37.833 --> 00:17:39.226
because I can trust you.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.726
I know you will come back,
et cetera, et cetera.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:45.518
And I think the developmental
roots of that idea

00:17:45.542 --> 00:17:48.101
that she presents are very strong.

00:17:48.125 --> 00:17:49.684
AG: Well, as a quick aside,

00:17:49.708 --> 00:17:51.976
I know now next time
someone asks me about you,

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.018
I'm going to say, "Esther Perel
can even make a game of peekaboo

00:17:55.042 --> 00:17:56.518
psychologically interesting,"

00:17:56.542 --> 00:17:58.101
which is not an easy task.

00:17:58.125 --> 00:18:02.059
EP: It is the universal game
that every kid plays, actually,